emma: Heads-up — I opened a docs PR to refresh the SDK snippets around streaming + pagination + retries for Py/TS/Go. Link: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/4234. Goal: provide small, runnable examples that show streaming + paginated results with sensible retry/backoff and an explicit migration note for the v2 pagination behavior. Can folks review for correctness and readability?

raj: Ack. I’ll add a TypeScript async-iterator example that shows exponential backoff + dedupe of partial tokens. Plan to include a compact helper `streamWithRetry`. Example sketch:
```ts
async function* streamWithRetry(req) {
  let tries = 0;
  while (tries < 3) {
    try {
      for await (const chunk of client.stream(req)) {
        yield chunk;
      }
      return;
    } catch (e) {
      tries++;
      await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 2**tries * 100));
    }
  }
  throw new Error('stream failed');
}
```
I’ll push a patch to the PR today.

morgan: Quick note for the Go snippet — avoid blocking channel sends in the example, show a small buffered channel and context cancellation. Also be explicit about `ResumeToken` usage for pagination (show where to persist / pass back). Suggested snippet: 
```go
ch := make(chan string, 8)
ctx, cancel := context.WithTimeout(context.Background(), 10*time.Second)
defer cancel()
go func() {
  defer close(ch)
  for res := range client.Stream(ctx, req) {
    select {
    case ch <- res.Token:
    case <-ctx.Done():
      return
    }
  }
}()
for t := range ch {
  fmt.Println(t)
}
```
Also add a one-line note: "For long-running streams persist the resume token after each checkpoint to enable exactly-once continuation."

sara: Thanks. For docs readability please keep each language example to ~8–12 lines; keep the migration note succinct and add a short before/after example for v1 -> v2 pagination behavior (i.e., `next_cursor` -> `resume_token`). Also please include an expected-stdout block for the small example — that helps non-dev readers verify quickly.

liam: Heads up — the docs auto-linker is currently keyed on the old anchor `#pagination` and we renamed the section to `#streaming-pagination`. I’ll update the auto-linker config but we should avoid adding stale anchors in the PR.

